WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
At the front of a large hall,
two singers start together:

2
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.070
one high, one low.

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.820
Each note travels as a
longitudinal wave through the air:

4
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.790
compressions and rarefactions,
heading for the back row.

5
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.890
The higher note has the higher frequency:

6
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.230
the air vibrates more times each second.

7
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.860
Does the higher note reach the
far side of the hall any sooner?

8
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.190
In this mission, you'll find out what
a wave carries from place to place.

9
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.860
Then you'll read wavelength, period and
amplitude off two graphs that look the

10
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.290
same but mean different things.

11
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.920
Your mission: predict whether
the higher note arrives sooner,

12
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.240
and explain why.
